        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "KW Quigg are delighted to bring Garryadeen, Grenagh, Co. Cork, to the market. \r\n\r\nThis impressive four-bedroom, two-bathroom detached bungalow offers approximately 150 sq. m. of well-proportioned accommodation, set on a superb half-acre site and enjoying truly spectacular panoramic views across the rolling hills and valleys of the surrounding Grenagh countryside. Garryadeen is a property that immediately stands out for its sense of space, privacy and connection with its surroundings. Sitting peacefully within the countryside, the home enjoys an elevated position with beautiful uninterrupted views, while remaining within easy reach of Blarney and Cork City. \r\n\r\nThe property opens into a welcoming entrance porch before leading into a generous and distinctive hallway which runs through the heart of the home. The layout is particularly practical, with the living and bedroom accommodation naturally flowing from the central hallway. The sitting room is a warm and inviting space, centred around an open fireplace which creates an attractive focal point and provides the perfect setting for relaxing. From here, the home opens into one of its most impressive features, a beautiful conservatory with a high timber ceiling and extensive glazing. Filled with natural light, this is a wonderful room from which to enjoy the property's private countryside outlook throughout the seasons. \r\n\r\nA return door provides direct access into the kitchen. The kitchen is a fantastic family space and enjoys some of the property's finest views. It is fitted with quality solid wood cabinetry, granite worktops and integrated appliances, while a working stove with back boiler adds both character and practical functionality. The generous layout provides plenty of space for cooking, dining and entertaining, with the countryside outlook making this a particularly enjoyable room in which to spend time. A large utility room is located directly off the kitchen and provides excellent additional storage and workspace, with convenient access to the rear of the property. \r\n\r\nThe accommodation continues with four generous bedrooms. The first three bedrooms are all well proportioned and offer excellent flexibility for family living, guests or working from home. The fourth bedroom, positioned to the rear of the property, is a particularly impressive master suite. The master bedroom is a beautiful private retreat, with French doors opening directly onto an elevated patio area. From here, the surrounding countryside can be enjoyed from an exceptional vantage point, creating a wonderful private outdoor space directly off the bedroom. The master bedroom is further complemented by a spacious ensuite with double shower, WC and wash hand basin. The main bathroom is also generously proportioned and features a bath, separate shower, WC and wash hand basin. \r\n\r\nOutside, Garryadeen sits on approximately half an acre of private grounds. The site provides an excellent balance of lawn, patio and storage areas, with two sheds providing valuable additional space. The elevated rear patio is undoubtedly one of the property's special features, offering a peaceful place to sit and enjoy the exceptional views over the Grenagh countryside. \r\n\r\nThe property also benefits from a number of excellent features including a BER rating of B, solar panels for hot water, oil-fired central heating, its own private well and a septic tank. The attic was partially converted during the original construction and benefits from three Velux windows, offering useful additional space and potential, subject to the necessary planning and building requirements. Fast internet connectivity is also available, making the property particularly suitable for modern family life and working from home. Despite its peaceful rural setting, Garryadeen is remarkably accessible. \r\n\r\nBlarney is approximately 10 minutes away, while Cork City is approximately 20 minutes from the property. This makes Garryadeen an ideal choice for those seeking the space, privacy and tranquillity of countryside living without being too far from the city. Garryadeen is a home that offers something increasingly difficult to find: generous accommodation, a substantial private site and exceptional countryside views, all within a convenient distance of Cork City. The combination of the property's setting, proportions and excellent living spaces makes this an outstanding opportunity for those looking for a quality family home in a peaceful rural environment. \r\n\r\nAccommodation \r\nRoom Dimensions Entrance Porch 2.3m x 2.3m \r\nSitting Room 5.1m x 3.6m \r\nConservatory 4m x 4m \r\nKitchen 6.6m x 4.5m \r\nUtility Room 2.8m x 2.4m \r\nBedroom 1 3.7m x 3m \r\nBedroom 2 3.6m x 4.3m \r\nBedroom 3 3.2m x 3m \r\nMain Bathroom 3.2m x 2.4m \r\nMaster Bedroom 5m x 4.4m \r\nEnsuite 3.2m x 1.3m \r\n\r\nProperty features \r\nBER B \r\nExceptional views \r\n½ acre site \r\nParking all around home \r\nAlarm fitted \r\nSolar panels for hot water \r\nNew rear raised patio with drainage \r\nRecently upgraded kitchen \r\nTurn key condition \r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the wonderful setting, privacy and views that Garryadeen has to offer. \r\n\r\nViewing by appointment only with auctioneer James Quigg 083 3820623"
      },
